OL,3,GNEWSAAsian hornet sting risk rising as
OL,4,Anests increase
OL,5,
OL,6,FAsian hornets are becoming a growing
OL,7,Fpublic safety threat in Jersey, with
OL,8,Fofficials warning that the likelihood
OL,9,Fof serious stings, including
OL,10,Flife-threatening reactions, is expected
OL,11,Fto rise.
OL,13,FThe first Asian hornets in the Channel
OL,14,FIslands were reported in Jersey in
OL,15,FAugust 2016. They arrived in Guernsey
OL,16,Fseven months later.
OL,18,FThe non-native invasive species is a
OL,19,Fpredator of other insects, including
OL,20,Fhoneybees, butterflies and beetles but
OL,21,Fits sting has also led to a number of
OL,22,Fhospital admissions.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
